# Build context hygiene.
#
# Without this file the context is ~42 MB, almost all of it .git history, test
# caches and byte-compiled Python that neither image copies. That cost is paid
# on every `docker build` -- including the one CI runs on every push -- and a
# stale __pycache__ landing in an image is a genuinely confusing failure.
#
# Both Dockerfiles copy an explicit, short list (pyproject.toml, README.md,
# src/, plus data/ for the API and ui/ for the frontend), so everything else is
# excluded here rather than trusted not to matter.

.git
.gitignore
.github

# Python build and cache artefacts
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.eggs/

# Virtualenvs
.venv/
venv/
env/

# Tooling caches
.pytest_cache/
.hypothesis/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
htmlcov/
mutants/

# Not needed at runtime
tests/
docs/
sample_output/
tasks.py

# Local configuration must never be baked into an image
.env
.envrc

# Editor and OS noise
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
